{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.shell_structure_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_structure_eigenvalues","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_structure_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_structure_eigenvalues","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/shell_structure_eigenvalues.lean#L87-L115","doc":"**Shell structure eigenvalues** (manuscript claims (i)–(iii)).\n\nThe orbital shell structure of an atom is governed by the eigenvalues of\nthe photon-electron transfer matrix\n`T_γe = !![q − q⁻¹, 1; 1, 0]`, whose characteristic polynomial is\n`λ² − (q − q⁻¹) λ − 1`.  Shell `n` corresponds to `T_γeⁿ`, whose entries\nare the Binet/Chebyshev sequence.\n\nThe single categorical input is that `λ_±` are the **two distinct roots**\nof the characteristic polynomial (existence of distinct real roots is the\nsubstrate-positivity fact `(q − q⁻¹)² + 4 > 0`).  Both Vieta relations\nand the Binet recurrence are then *derived*:\n\n* (i) `λ_+ · λ_- = −1`         (Vieta product = constant coefficient);\n* (ii) `λ_+ + λ_- = q − q⁻¹`   (Vieta sum = linear coefficient);\n* (iii) the matrix-power entries `(Tⁿ)_{21} = binet n` satisfy the\n  second-kind Chebyshev recurrence `U_{n+1} = (q−q⁻¹) U_n + U_{n−1}`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:shell-structure-eigenvalues","label":"prop:shell-structure-eigenvalues","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-structure-eigenvalues.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.binet_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.binet_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/shell_structure_eigenvalues.lean#L63-L85","doc":"The Binet sequence satisfies the second-order linear recurrence\n`binet (n+2) = s · binet (n+1) + binet n` whenever `λ_±` are roots of\n`λ² − s λ − 1` (so `λ_±² = s λ_± + 1`).  Derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.binet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.binet","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/shell_structure_eigenvalues.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The Binet closed form for the matrix-power entries.  `binet n =\n(λ_+ⁿ − λ_-ⁿ)/(λ_+ − λ_-)` — the second-kind Chebyshev sequence\n`U_{n-1}` in the variable `(q − q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_sum","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/shell_structure_eigenvalues.lean#L45-L55","doc":"**Vieta sum.** If `λ_±` are distinct roots of `λ² − s λ − 1 = 0`,\ntheir sum is `s` (the linear coefficient). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_eigenvalue_product","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/shell_structure_eigenvalues.lean#L26-L43","doc":"**Vieta product.** If `λ_±` are roots of `λ² − s λ − 1 = 0`, their\nproduct is `−1` (the constant coefficient).  Derived from the two\nroot equations together with `λ_+ ≠ λ_-`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}